\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Behold, the mountain of the Lord
\par In latter days shall rise
\par On mountain- tops above the hills,
\par And draw the wondering eyes.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. To this the joyful nations round,
\par All tribes and tongues, shall flow;
\par Up to the hill of God, they' ll say,
\par And to His house, we'll go.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. The beam that shines from Zion's hill
\par Shall lighten every land;
\par The King who reigns in Salem's towers
\par Shall all the world command.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Among the nations He shall judge;
\par His judgements truth shall guide;
\par His sceptre shall protect the just,
\par And quell the sinner's pride.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. No strife shall rage, nor hostile feuds
\par Disturb those peaceful years;
\par To ploughshares men shall beat their swords,
\par To pruning- hooks their spears.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. No longer hosts, encountering hosts,
\par Shall crowds of slain deplore,
\par They hang the trumpet in the hall,
\par And study war no more.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 7\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 7. Come then, O house of Jacob, come
\par To worship at His shrine;
\par And, walking in the light of God,
\par With holy beauties shine.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

